        "title": "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "1d67db6a-7337-599e-8ecc-26284642ae3b",
        ":question/problem": "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=\u27e8y{e}^{x},\\,x-{e}^{x}\u27e9$\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=\u27e82y,\\,x\u27e9$\n\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=\u27e8-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1\u27e9$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=\u27e8P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)\u27e9,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={\u222c}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}(\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222e}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}={e}^{x}$\nand\n$\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}=1-{e}^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=1-2{e}^{x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=2$\nand\n$\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}=\\frac{2}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
